## 🔬 Target Hardware Alignment

TeleShield features hardware-aware quantum simulation profiles with parameters derived from published experimental literature:

| Profile | Target Physics | Primary Backend | Gate Fidelity (1Q / 2Q) | Readout Fidelity | Memory $T_2$ | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `ideal.yaml` | Mathematical Limit | Exact NumPy | 1.0 / 1.0 | 1.0 | $\infty$ | Zero-noise reference model |
| `ion_trap.yaml` | Trapped-Ion Gates ($^{171}\text{Yb}^+$ / $^{40}\text{Ca}^+$) | Qiskit Aer | 0.9998 / 0.9950 | 0.9960 | 1.50 s | Literature-derived ion-trap profile |
| `rydberg.yaml` | Neutral-Atom Rydberg Arrays ($^{87}\text{Rb}$) | Pulser / Aer | 0.9990 / 0.9850 | 0.9800 | 0.05 s | Literature-derived neutral-atom profile |

> **Hardware Disclaimer**: TeleShield provides *ion-trap-aligned* and *Rydberg-aligned* simulation profiles based on literature-derived parameters. They do not claim or reproduce proprietary commercial hardware specifications.

